From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: batch NPU receive completion work

The NPU RX loop calls mt76_rx_poll_complete after every skb, including
control notifications which queue no data frames. That repeatedly acquires
the device-wide rx_lock and dispatches short lists to mac80211.

Complete the bounded poll batch once, as the regular DMA RX path already
does. Preserve delivery order and finish upper-layer work before refilling
the ring and completing NAPI. Zero-budget polls and provider RCU lifetime
remain unchanged. NPU/PPE acceleration and hardware queue sizes are
retained.

Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>

--- a/npu.c
+++ b/npu.c
@@ -251,10 +251,12 @@
 		}
 
 		dev->drv->rx_skb(dev, qid, skb, &info);
-		mt76_rx_poll_complete(dev, qid, napi);
 		done++;
 	}
 
+	if (done)
+		mt76_rx_poll_complete(dev, qid, napi);
+
 	mt76_npu_fill_rx_queue(dev, q);
 out:
 	if (done < budget && napi_complete(napi))
